/-! # L7-middle M5 — `hrep` at the σ̃ contour: pointwise ⟹ integral

`zeta2-l7-middle.md` §7 row M5, built on M4 (`L7MidM4.theorem5B_ordinate`), M2's analyticity
(`L7MidM123.differentiableOn_Hn`), the generic measure theory of `L7MidM5Probe`, and C6/X-L7.
Everything is elaborated in the CONSOLIDATED file, so `theorem5B_ordinate` and
`differentiableOn_Hn` are consumed for real and the final theorem applies the REAL
`Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate` (`skills/LEAN.md` §3).

**What this row closes.**  `routeB_l7_rate` entered the day with seven hypotheses; the C7 row
discharged six of them as numeric facts, leaving `hrep` — L7 Theorem 5 composed with the
identification of `r_n` as a line integral.  `hrep` was M4 + M5 + M6, and this is M5:
`‖H_n‖ ≤ e^{C_B}·e^{n g(|s|/n)}` pointwise on `Re t = −σ̃n − ½` becomes

  `|r_n| ≤ (n/π)·e^{C_B}·∫_{(0,∞)} e^{n g(w)} dw`,

which is `hrep` verbatim, at `C := C_B` and `c := kappaPi`.

**Three things this row had to decide, all recorded as theorems rather than as remarks.**

1. **`r_n` must be NAMED.**  `hrep` is a statement *about* `r`, universally quantified in
   `routeB_l7_rate`, so discharging it requires a definition.  `rIntC` is
   `zeta2-l7-proof.md` §1's `(1/2πi)∫_{Re t = −σ̃n−½} H_n(t) dt` after `t = c + is`,
   `dt = i ds` — the `i`'s cancel and what is left is `(1/2π)∫_ℝ H_n(c + is) ds`.  It is
   COMPLEX; the chain wants a real sequence, so `rLine n := (rIntC n).re` and the bridge is
   `Complex.abs_re_le_norm`, one step, no realness proof.  The arithmetic identification
   `r_n = q_n ζ(2) − p_n` is L1/A2 and is deliberately NOT on this row's path
   (`zeta2-l7-middle.md` §5); `hrep_of_le_norm` is stated so that whoever does it inherits the
   bound for the real `r_n` without reopening anything here.

2. **INTEGRABILITY IS DERIVED, from the SAME two C6 facts `integral_exp_phase_le` already
   consumes.**  This row introduces no hypothesis of its own: `hsup`/`htail` come out of
   `Zeta2SupScheme.routeB_ingredients`, which is what `routeB_l7_rate` calls anyway, so the
   final theorem stands on the six C7 numeric facts and nothing else.

3. **The `∫`-junk value, and why 2 is not optional.**  Lean's `∫` of a non-integrable function
   is `0`.  So `hrep`'s right-hand side is not automatically positive: without the tail decay
   it would read `|r_n| ≤ 0`.  `L7MidM5Probe.hrep_rhs_is_junk_without_decay` exhibits that at
   the constant phase.  This is the FOURTH junk-value trap measured in this program — after
   `Real.log 0 = 0` (M4's acceptance clause, and X-L7's two `limsup` falsifiers) — and it is on
   the other side of the same inequality.  The same reasoning is why `integrable_Hn_lineB` is
   proved rather than skipped: without it `rIntC n` could itself be the junk value `0`, and the
   deliverable would be a true statement about a meaningless object.
-/

namespace L7MidM5

open L7MidM123 L7MidM4 Zeta2SupScheme MeasureTheory

/-! ## §1. The contour in the write-up's ordinate, and `r_n` -/

/-- The route-B contour point in `zeta2-l7-proof.md` §1's own ordinate: `t = −σ̃n − ½ + i s`.
`contourB` (M4) is the same line parameterised by the SCALED ordinate `v = s/n`, and
`lineB_eq_contourB` is the bridge — which is why M5's change of variables is a rewrite. -/
noncomputable def lineB (n : ℕ) (s : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  ((-(sigT * (n : ℝ)) - 1 / 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) + (s : ℂ) * Complex.I

/-- `lineB n s = contourB n (s/n)` — M4's `contourB_ordinate`, read the other way. -/
theorem lineB_eq_contourB {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) (s : ℝ) :
    lineB n s = contourB n (s / (n : ℝ)) := (contourB_ordinate hn s).symm

/-- `lineB n` is continuous — needed to know the integrand is measurable, hence that `rIntC`
below is a genuine integral rather than Lean's junk value. -/
theorem continuous_lineB (n : ℕ) : Continuous (lineB n) := by
  unfold lineB
  exact continuous_const.add (Complex.continuous_ofReal.mul continuous_const)

/-- The contour lies in M2's closed strip, at its LEFT edge, for every `n`.  `σ̃ > 4` is what
puts it strictly left of route A's `Re t = −4n − ½` (M4's `strip_nonempty`), and `σ̃ ≤ 9` is
what `differentiableOn_Hn` spends. -/
theorem lineB_mem_Strip (n : ℕ) (s : ℝ) : lineB n s ∈ Strip n sigT := by
  have hnn : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (n : ℝ) := Nat.cast_nonneg n
  have hre : (lineB n s).re = -(sigT * (n : ℝ)) - 1 / 2 := by simp [lineB]
  have h4 : (4 : ℝ) < sigT := by norm_num [sigT]
  have hprod : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (sigT - 4) * (n : ℝ) := mul_nonneg (by linarith) hnn
  exact ⟨by rw [hre]; nlinarith, by rw [hre]; nlinarith⟩

/-- **`H_n` restricted to the contour is CONTINUOUS**, straight from M2's manifest analyticity
on the closed strip.  `zeta2-l7-middle.md` §3b's whole point: no pole census, no removable
singularity — the reflected definition is differentiable on the closed strip and the contour is
one of its edges. -/
theorem continuous_Hn_lineB (n : ℕ) : Continuous fun s : ℝ => Hn n (lineB n s) :=
  ((differentiableOn_Hn n (by norm_num [sigT] : sigT ≤ 9)).continuousOn).comp_continuous
    (continuous_lineB n) (lineB_mem_Strip n)

/-- **`r_n`, as `zeta2-l7-proof.md` §1 defines it.**  `(1/2πi) ∫_{Re t = −σ̃n−½} H_n(t) dt` with
`t = −σ̃n − ½ + is` and `dt = i ds`: the two `i`'s cancel and what remains is a real-line
integral with the prefactor `1/2π`.  That cancellation is where `hrep`'s `n/π` comes from —
`(1/2π) · 2n = n/π` — and it is checked independently in `margins_m5.py` §1. -/
noncomputable def rIntC (n : ℕ) : ℂ :=
  (1 / (2 * Real.pi) : ℂ) * ∫ s : ℝ, Hn n (lineB n s)

/-- The real sequence the chain consumes.  `H_n`'s line integral is real (it is
`q_n ζ(2) − p_n`), but that is L1/A2's identification and this row does not need it: taking the
real part costs one `Complex.abs_re_le_norm` and leaves the identification free to land later
against `hrep_of_le_norm`, which is stated for ANY real sequence dominated by `‖rIntC‖`.

Named `rLine` — the real part of the σ̃-contour LINE integral — and not `rB`, since 2026-09-10:
the capstone's conclusion also carries C7's bracket radius `Zeta2C7.rB = 10⁻⁹`, and two `rB`s in
one statement read as one thing (arch-sweep residue named by the C7/M5 units). -/
noncomputable def rLine (n : ℕ) : ℝ := (rIntC n).re

/-! ## §2. The pointwise bound, transported to the ordinate -/

/-- Route B's phase is continuous — `Zeta2L7Assembly.phase_continuous` at the certified
parameters, needed by the integrability argument. -/
theorem phaseB_continuous :
    Continuous (phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi) :=
  Zeta2L7Assembly.phase_continuous _ _ _ _ _ qB_pos (by norm_num [sigT])

/-- M4's `theorem5B_ordinate`, in `lineB`'s vocabulary.  The `|s| / n` is `zeta2-l7-proof.md`
§6's substitution together with the evenness of the bound; `L7MidM4.phase_neg_arg` is why the
absolute value cannot be dropped. -/
theorem norm_Hn_lineB_le {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) (s : ℝ) :
    ‖Hn n (lineB n s)‖
      ≤ Real.exp C_B
        * Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi (|s| / (n : ℝ))) := by
  simp only [lineB]
  exact theorem5B_ordinate hn s

/-- **The integrand of `r_n` is INTEGRABLE** — so `rIntC` is a genuine integral and not Lean's
junk value `0`.  Derived, not assumed: continuity (M2) supplies measurability and the pointwise
bound (M4) supplies the dominating function, whose own integrability is
`L7MidM5Probe.integrable_exp_phase_line` from the two C6 facts.

Without this, every theorem below would still be TRUE and would say nothing: a bound on `|r_n|`
where `r_n` is definitionally `0` is not a rate. -/
theorem integrable_Hn_lineB {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) {G c₀ : ℝ} (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hsup : ∀ w : ℝ, 0 ≤ w → phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G)
    (htail : ∀ w : ℝ, 3 ≤ w →
      phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G - c₀ * (w - 3)) :
    Integrable (fun s : ℝ => Hn n (lineB n s)) volume := by
  have hnpos : (0 : ℝ) < (n : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast hn
  refine Integrable.mono'
    ((L7MidM5Probe.integrable_exp_phase_line phaseB_continuous hnpos hc₀ hsup htail).const_mul
      (Real.exp C_B))
    (continuous_Hn_lineB n).aestronglyMeasurable ?_
  filter_upwards with s
  exact norm_Hn_lineB_le hn s

/-! ## §3. THE FOLD — `∫_ℝ` onto `∫_{(0,∞)}`, and `hrep` -/

/-- **M5's master bound.**  `‖r_n‖ ≤ (n/π)·e^{C_B}·∫_{(0,∞)} e^{n g(w)} dw`.

The three steps of `zeta2-l7-middle.md` §7 M5, all inside `L7MidM5Probe.norm_line_integral_le`:
`‖∫‖ ≤ ∫‖·‖`, then M4's pointwise bound under `integral_mono_of_nonneg` against the derived
dominating function, then `integral_comp_abs` (the `∫_ℝ → 2∫_{Ioi 0}` fold, which is where the
evenness in `|s|` is spent) and `integral_comp_mul_left_Ioi` (the `s = n w` substitution, which
is where the surviving factor of `n` comes from). -/
theorem norm_rIntC_le {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) {G c₀ : ℝ} (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hsup : ∀ w : ℝ, 0 ≤ w → phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G)
    (htail : ∀ w : ℝ, 3 ≤ w →
      phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G - c₀ * (w - 3)) :
    ‖rIntC n‖ ≤ (n : ℝ) * (Real.exp C_B / Real.pi)
      * ∫ w in Set.Ioi (0 : ℝ),
          Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w) := by
  have hnpos : (0 : ℝ) < (n : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast hn
  simp only [rIntC]
  exact L7MidM5Probe.norm_line_integral_le phaseB_continuous hnpos hc₀ hsup htail
    (fun s => norm_Hn_lineB_le hn s)

/-- **`hrep`, for any real sequence dominated by the line integral.**  Stated with exactly the
hypothesis its future caller PRODUCES (`LEAN.md` §3's corollary): the row that formalizes
`r_n = q_n ζ(2) − p_n` will have `|r_n| = ‖rIntC n‖` (or `≤`), and hands it straight in.  Until
then `rLine` below is the witness that the interface is inhabited. -/
theorem hrep_of_le_norm {ρ : ℕ → ℝ} {G c₀ : ℝ} (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hsup : ∀ w : ℝ, 0 ≤ w → phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G)
    (htail : ∀ w : ℝ, 3 ≤ w →
      phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G - c₀ * (w - 3))
    (hρ : ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → |ρ n| ≤ ‖rIntC n‖) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → |ρ n| ≤ (n : ℝ) * (Real.exp C_B / Real.pi)
      * ∫ w in Set.Ioi (0 : ℝ),
          Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w) :=
  fun n hn => le_trans (hρ n hn) (norm_rIntC_le hn hc₀ hsup htail)

/-- **`hrep` — the row's target, VERBATIM as `Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate` states it**, at
`C := C_B` and `c := kappaPi`. -/
theorem hrep_rLine {G c₀ : ℝ} (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hsup : ∀ w : ℝ, 0 ≤ w → phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G)
    (htail : ∀ w : ℝ, 3 ≤ w →
      phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G - c₀ * (w - 3)) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → |rLine n| ≤ (n : ℝ) * (Real.exp C_B / Real.pi)
      * ∫ w in Set.Ioi (0 : ℝ),
          Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w) :=
  hrep_of_le_norm hc₀ hsup htail (fun _n _ => Complex.abs_re_le_norm _)

/-! ## §4. THE COMPOSITION, EXECUTED (`LEAN.md` §3)

Proving `hrep` "with `routeB_l7_rate` as a consumer" composes on paper.  The theorem below is
the composition run: it applies the REAL `Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate` with `hrep` supplied,
so the kernel checks that what M5 proved is what X-L7 assumes. -/

/-- **THE ROW'S DELIVERABLE.**  `Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate` with `hrep` DISCHARGED: the
chain's L7 interface for the explicit `r` of §1, standing on the six C7 numeric facts
(`hbl`, `hbr`, `hε₀`, `hG`, `h3`, `hs3`) and nothing else.

`hrr`, `hc₀`, `hε` are not facts to discharge — they are the positivity of the bracket radius,
of the tail slope and of `ε`, all supplied by the caller at the certified witnesses
(`r = 10⁻⁹`, `c₀ = 4/5`).  So the honest count is: **seven hypotheses in, one closed here, six
left, and all six are C7's.** -/
theorem routeB_l7_rate_hrep_discharged {ws rr ε₀ G c₀ : ℝ} (hrr : 0 ≤ rr) (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hbl : 0 ≤ phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 (ws - rr))
    (hbr : phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 (ws + rr) ≤ 0)
    (hε₀ : |phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 ws| ≤ ε₀)
    (hG : phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi ws ≤ G)
    (h3 : phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi 3 ≤ G + ε₀ * rr)
    (hs3 : phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 3 ≤ -c₀)
    {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop, |rLine n| ≤ Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * ((G + ε₀ * rr) + ε)) := by
  obtain ⟨hs, ht⟩ := routeB_ingredients kappaPi hrr hbl hbr hε₀ hG h3 hs3
  exact Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate (rn := rLine) kappaPi hrr hc₀ hbl hbr hε₀ hG h3 hs3
    (hrep_rLine hc₀ hs ht) hε

/-- The same composition for an ARBITRARY real `r_n` dominated by the line integral — the shape
the arithmetic-identification row will use, so that row never has to reopen M5. -/
theorem routeB_l7_rate_of_le_norm {ρ : ℕ → ℝ} {ws rr ε₀ G c₀ : ℝ} (hrr : 0 ≤ rr) (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hbl : 0 ≤ phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 (ws - rr))
    (hbr : phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 (ws + rr) ≤ 0)
    (hε₀ : |phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 ws| ≤ ε₀)
    (hG : phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi ws ≤ G)
    (h3 : phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi 3 ≤ G + ε₀ * rr)
    (hs3 : phaseD Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 3 ≤ -c₀)
    (hρ : ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → |ρ n| ≤ ‖rIntC n‖)
    {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop, |ρ n| ≤ Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * ((G + ε₀ * rr) + ε)) := by
  obtain ⟨hs, ht⟩ := routeB_ingredients kappaPi hrr hbl hbr hε₀ hG h3 hs3
  exact Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate (rn := ρ) kappaPi hrr hc₀ hbl hbr hε₀ hG h3 hs3
    (hrep_of_le_norm hc₀ hs ht hρ) hε

/-! ## §5. EDGE CASES (`LEAN.md` §5) — asked of the statement, not of the proof -/

/-- **EDGE, `n = 1`: the binding instance.**  Instantiated rather than asserted, so a change
that broke the `n = 1` case would red this line rather than sit in a green file. -/
example {G c₀ : ℝ} (hc₀ : 0 < c₀)
    (hsup : ∀ w : ℝ, 0 ≤ w → phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G)
    (htail : ∀ w : ℝ, 3 ≤ w →
      phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w ≤ G - c₀ * (w - 3)) :
    |rLine 1| ≤ ((1 : ℕ) : ℝ) * (Real.exp C_B / Real.pi)
      * ∫ w in Set.Ioi (0 : ℝ),
          Real.exp (((1 : ℕ) : ℝ) * phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi w) :=
  hrep_rLine hc₀ hsup htail 1 le_rfl

/-- **EDGE, `n = 0`, and the answer is that `1 ≤ n` is load-bearing in the STATEMENT.**
`hrep`'s right-hand side carries a leading factor `(n : ℝ)`, so at `n = 0` it is `0` whatever
the integral does — the clause would read `|r 0| ≤ 0`, an unproved (and almost certainly false)
claim about `r 0`, not a rate.  Two independent mechanisms would have to be repaired, not one:
this factor, and `L7MidM4.n_zero_blocked_by_M3`'s failure of the `Π(n)` bound at `n = 0`. -/
theorem hrep_rhs_zero_at_zero (I : ℝ) : ((0 : ℕ) : ℝ) * (Real.exp C_B / Real.pi) * I = 0 := by
  simp

/-- **EDGE, the ordinate at `n = 0`, and it is a FIFTH junk value.**  `zeta2-l7-proof.md` §6's
substitution is `w = s/n`; in Lean `x / 0 = 0`, so at `n = 0` the whole real line maps to the
single point `w = 0` and M4's bound degenerates to a constant.  Recorded because the `n = 0`
asymmetry in this row is *two* separate collapses (see above) and only one of them is visible
from M3.  Junk-value census for this program: `Real.log 0 = 0` (M4, X-L7 ×2),
`∫ (non-integrable) = 0` (`L7MidM5Probe` §4), `x / 0 = 0` (here). -/
theorem ordinate_collapses_at_zero (s : ℝ) : |s| / ((0 : ℕ) : ℝ) = 0 := by simp

/-- **EDGE, `s = 0`.**  The one point of the contour where `zeta2-l7-proof.md`'s kernel form
`(π/sin πt)²` would not exist if `σ̃n + ½` were an integer.  In the reflected form the bound
holds there with no case split (M4's own `w = 0` edge), and here that point is a null set of
the `s`-integral in any case — so the odd-`q̃` argument `zeta2-l7-middle.md` §3a retired stays
retired through the integration step too. -/
example {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
    ‖Hn n (lineB n 0)‖
      ≤ Real.exp C_B
        * Real.exp ((n : ℝ) * phase Finset.univ qB (26 - sigT) 1 kappaPi (|(0 : ℝ)| / (n : ℝ))) :=
  norm_Hn_lineB_le hn 0

